# The DAC on channel 6 (0x2B bit 7), against FM: channels 1 to 5 play soft
# notes and channel 6 a loud one; the DAC then replaces channel 6 with a
# sawtooth written through 0x2A (the 8 high bits, offset binary) with the
# low bit from 0x2C bit 3; channel 6's panning (0x1B6) routes it left, right
# and nowhere; a 0x2A write on the upper port goes to the FM registers
# instead; and the DAC is disabled again.
